      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In Japan and worldwide, the increase in educational interventions about resuscitation training significantly increases favorable neurological survival in out-of-hospital cardiopulmonary arrest cases treated with bystander cardiopulmonary resuscitation (BCPR) each year. This case with Bland-White-Garland syndrome having high-quality BCPR by nurses demonstrates the importance of education about BCPR."},
